{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"list_data_products","title":"List Data Products","description":"Discover all available real-time data views (data products) that represent business entities like customers, orders, products, etc. Each data product provides fresh, queryable data with defined schemas. Use this first to see what data is available before querying specific information.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"get_data_product_details","title":"Get Data Product Details","description":"Get one data product's columns and how to read it. `read.cluster` is the cluster to pass to `query`: the cluster your role can use with an index on the product, preferring a hydrated index. A null `read.cluster` means the product is a materialized view with no index your role can use: omit `cluster`, and the query returns its stored results. `read.uses_index` says whether the read is served from an index. `read.hydration` (`{hydrated, replica_count, hydrated_replica_count}`) describes that read. Reads never return partial data: if `hydrated` is false and `replica_count` is greater than 0, wait and retry. If `replica_count` is 0, the read cannot make progress until a replica is added. `read.faster_read_available` is true when an index on the product exists on a cluster your role cannot use.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"Exact name of the data product from list_data_products() list"}},"required":["name"]},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"query","title":"Query","description":"Execute a read-only SQL query (SELECT, SHOW, or EXPLAIN) against any object the role can access, including data products and the system catalog. Pass the cluster from the data product details so indexed reads hit the arrangement. Omit `cluster` to run on your session's default cluster, for example when the data product's cluster is null. Write system object names in full, such as `mz_catalog.mz_clusters`. Response limit: 1.0 MB.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"cluster":{"type":"string","description":"Exact cluster name the query should run on, such as the cluster from the data product details. Omit it to run on your session's default cluster. EXPLAIN ANALYZE needs a cluster."},"cluster_replica":{"type":"string","description":"Optional replica name (e.g. 'r1') to target one replica of `cluster`. Requires `cluster`. Required for EXPLAIN ANALYZE on clusters with more than one replica. Find replica names in mz_catalog.mz_cluster_replicas."},"sql_query":{"type":"string","description":"PostgreSQL-compatible SELECT, SHOW, or EXPLAIN statement. Use the fully qualified data product name exactly as provided (with double quotes). Multi-statement queries are rejected."}},"required":["sql_query"]},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}}]}}

